  <data key="d9">Risk Management and Compliance for an Insurance Company.docx</data>
  <data key="d10">Risk Management &amp; Compliance Manual</data>
  <data key="d11">Board Approval: The Board of Directors reviews and approves the risk appetite and tolerance levels annually. This ensures alignment with the company's overall risk management strategy and strategic objectives, fostering a unified approach to managing risk.</data>
</node>
<node id="chunk:dd8ee0e795da">
  <data key="d0">policy_chunk</data>
  <data key="d9">Risk Management and Compliance for an Insurance Company.docx</data>
  <data key="d10">Risk Management &amp; Compliance Manual</data>
  <data key="d11">Board Role: The Board of Directors provides oversight and guidance on capital management and compliance efforts, ensuring alignment with SecureLife's strategic objectives and regulatory requirements. This oversight supports effective governance and risk management.</data>
</node>
<node id="chunk:f28ab5c4ff30">
  <data key="d0">policy_chunk</data>
  <data key="d9">Risk Management and Compliance for an Insurance Company.docx</data>
  <data key="d10">Risk Management &amp; Compliance Manual</data>
  <data key="d11">Board Oversight: The Board of Directors provides oversight and guidance on capital management and compliance efforts, ensuring alignment with SecureLife's strategic objectives and regulatory requirements. This oversight supports effective governance and risk management.</data>
</node>
<node id="chunk:a6f05eadc236">
  <data key="d0">policy_chunk</data>
  <data key="d9">Risk Management and Compliance for an Insurance Company.docx</data>
  <data key="d10">Risk Management &amp; Compliance Manual</data>
  <data key="d11">Monitoring: A monitoring system is in place to track risk exposures against risk appetite and tolerance levels. Any breaches are promptly identified and reported to senior management and the Board, allowing for timely corrective action.</data>
</node>
<node id="chunk:ed1dc9ae6582">
  <data key="d0">policy_chunk</data>
  <data key="d9">Risk Management and Compliance for an Insurance Company.docx</data>
  <data key="d10">Risk Management &amp; Compliance Manual</data>
  <data key="d11">Board Oversight: The Board of Directors oversees the solvency assessment process, providing guidance and oversight to ensure alignment with SecureLife's strategic objectives and regulatory requirements. This oversight ensures that solvency assessments are conducted rigorously and objectively.</data>
</node>
<node id="chunk:b21a82407a61">
  <data key="d0">policy_chunk</data>
  <data key="d9">Risk Management and Compliance for an Insurance Company.docx</data>
  <data key="d10">Risk Management &amp; Compliance Manual</data>
  <data key="d11">Performance Monitoring: The performance of the reinsurance program is continuously monitored, assessing its impact on risk exposure, capital requirements, and financial performance. SecureLife conducts semi-annual reviews to evaluate the effectiveness of reinsurance arrangements.</data>
</node>
